/-!
# Positive coefficient-canonical twists on the full exceptional curve

The original exceptional ideal powers are generated by the actual projective
coordinate sections through a supplied original O(1) pullback comparison.
Their original quotient section modules have dimension at least two by the
height theorem. Original structural constants therefore prevent any positive
power from being trivial. Coefficient Serre duality gives the H1 vanishing.

The curve is the full, possibly nonreduced exceptional scheme; the residue
field is arbitrary and the coefficient line is not identified with that field.
The embedding and original O(1) comparison are explicit geometric suppliers.
This is not a global-generation theorem for the coefficient canonical twist.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory
